description:
Implement EventSource subscription in app.js: subscribe to /jmap/events, on state events call /changes to fetch deltas and update UI.

What: Open EventSource, on 'state' events call Message/changes and Chat/changes, merge results into local state, re-render.

Algorithm:
1. function buildEventsUrl():
   - Start from session.eventsUrl template (from JMAP session object)
   - Replace {types} with 'Message,Chat', {closeafter} with 'no', {ping} with ''
   - Result: https://host/jmap/events?types=Message,Chat&closeafter=no&ping=
2. function startEventSource():
   - const url = buildEventsUrl();
   - const es = new EventSource(url);
   - es.addEventListener('state', handleStateEvent);
   - es.onerror = () => { console.error('EventSource disconnected, will reconnect'); };
   - Browser reconnects automatically with Last-Event-ID
3. async function handleStateEvent(event):
   - const data = JSON.parse(event.data);
   - const changed = data.changed['a-self'];  // { 'Message': 's-N', 'Chat': 's-M' }
   - if (changed.Message && currentChatId):
     - const responses = await callJmap([['Message/changes', { accountId: 'a-self', sinceState: messageState }, 'mc0']]);
     - const [, result] = responses[0];
     - if (result.type === 'cannotCalculateChanges') { await fetchMessages(currentChatId); return; }
     - if (result.created.length > 0):
       - Fetch new messages: Message/get with result.created as ids
       - Append new message bubbles to thread
     - messageState = result.newState;
   - if (changed.Chat):
     - const responses = await callJmap([['Chat/changes', { accountId: 'a-self', sinceState: chatState }, 'cc0']]);
     - const [, result] = responses[0];
     - if (result.type === 'cannotCalculateChanges') { await fetchChats(); return; }
     - chatState = result.newState;
     - Re-fetch affected chats and re-render chat list
4. Call startEventSource() in renderApp() after initial data load.
5. Update unread count in chat list for non-active chats when new messages arrive.

Defensive programming rules:
- Always handle 'cannotCalculateChanges' (server dropped state) by re-fetching all.
- Parse JSON in try/catch — malformed event must not crash the app.
- Never innerHTML for any received data.
- Store messageState and chatState after every successful /changes call.
- EventSource URL is a template — replace all three placeholders before using.

Tests (oracle: EventSource event format from kithd/src/events.rs + RFC 8620 §7.3):
- Given event data '{"changed":{"a-self":{"Message":"s-5"}}}', handleStateEvent calls Message/changes with sinceState=prior state
- Given Message/changes returns created=['msg-id-1'], new bubble is appended to thread
- Given Message/changes returns type='cannotCalculateChanges', falls back to fetchMessages
- EventSource .onerror does not crash app, logs to console
